@model Profile
@*
    The hero's animated background (ADR-0008): lanes of scrolling code from the owner's own
    stack, with a few quiet technology logos scattered over it. It is the stronger twin of the
    faint layer fixed behind the rest of the page (see _Layout.cshtml); both use the same lanes
    so the background looks continuous. Purely decorative, so it is hidden from assistive
    technology and never takes pointer events.

    The technologies are shared between the two layers so each logo appears once: this layer
    takes the first TechLogoData.HeroLogoCount of Profile.BackdropTags and the page layer takes
    the rest. A content test requires every tag to appear in the projects, roles or skills and
    to have a logo, so the background can never advertise a technology the page does not back
    up (ADR-0006).
*@
@using Portfolio.Web.Content
@{
    var heroTechs = Model.BackdropTags.Take(TechLogoData.HeroLogoCount).ToList();
}
<div class="code-backdrop" aria-hidden="true">
    <partial name="_CodeStreams" model="@("hero")" />
    <partial name="_TechLogos" model="heroTechs" view-data="@(new ViewDataDictionary(ViewData) { { "variant", "hero" } })" />
</div>
